    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule so that creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` following the same pattern as the existing `DuplicateHouseholdException`/`DuplicateTelephoneException`, carrying the offending city.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a capacity check after the existing validations (missing fields, duplicate telephone, duplicate household). It throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the target city is at capacity. The check is backed by a new `isCityAtCapacity(city)` helper and a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant; city comparison reuses the existing `normalizeIdentity` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed), consistent with the controller's other city/name logic.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityAtCapacityException` returning **409 Conflict** with a ProblemDetail whose `errors` array names the `city` field, mirroring the other 409 handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a city to 50, then expect the 51st to be rejected) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
